# Unit Tests (Clean Code Ch.9)

## FIRST

Fast, Independent, Repeatable, Self-validating, Timely.

## AAA

Arrange / Act / Assert. One concept per test. Names say behavior.

## Dual standard

Production size/complexity gates stay strict. Spec and harness files may relax max-lines / complexity / max-classes — keep naming and “no empty catch” discipline.

## Harness / DSL

Put DOM trains, fixture setup, and resume content fixtures in `*.harness.*` (or a `test/fixtures` module) — not inline in every `it`. Prefer `rejects.toThrow` / idiomatic assertion APIs over try/catch for expected failures.

## Coverage

Prefer meaningful tests over chasing percentage alone. Wire coverage in CI when a test runner (Vitest or Jest) is added to this repo.
